"chronology","label":"F2 material incorrect, unsupported or misleading","evidence":"We achieved this by splitting our fortnightly sprints in two: testing, researching and accepting applications in the first week and then suspending submissions to concentrate on testing, researching and processing applications the second.","narrative":"tijdens de private beta wisselden tweewekelijkse sprints af tussen aanvragen aannemen en tijd besteden aan testen, onderzoek en verwerking","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source describes splitting each fortnightly sprint into two weeks, not alternating fortnight-long sprints.","materiality":"It changes the cadence of the team’s working method."},{"excerpt":"In de ene periode werden aanvragen aangenomen; in de andere was tijd gereserveerd voor testen, onderzoek en verwerking.","claim":"The team accepted applications in one period and reserved the other for testing, research and processing, implying those activities were separated into alternating periods.","category":"technical","label":"F2 material incorrect, unsupported or misleading","evidence":"testing, researching and accepting applications in the first week and then suspending submissions to concentrate on testing, researching and processing applications the second","narrative":"tussen aanvragen aannemen en tijd besteden aan testen, onderzoek en verwerking","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source says testing and research happened in both weeks; applications were accepted in the first week, while submissions were suspended in the second for testing, research and processing. The piece’s contrast suggests testing and research were confined to the other period.","materiality":"It misrepresents how activities were distributed across the two weeks."},{"excerpt":"Zo zag het werkritme eruit: eerst de aanvragerservaring, met binnen de beta ook vaste ruimte voor onderzoek en testen.","claim":"The team’s approach prioritized the applicants’ experience and included scheduled time for research and testing during private beta.","category":"other","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"My team focused on the users applying for refunds first and this is what we took to the alpha assessment.\n\nWe achieved this by splitting our fortnightly sprints in two: testing, researching and accepting applications in the first week and then suspending submissions to concentrate on testing, researching and processing applications the second.","narrative":"De beschreven aanpak combineerde een volgorde waarin aanvragers eerst kwamen met expliciet gereserveerde tijd voor onderzoek en testen.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source supports both the priority given to applicants and the planned testing and research time during beta; this summary does not claim that either caused the launch or any results.","materiality":"It summarizes the approach described in the source."}]}

